            <p>Erythrolakia, Posterior Aspect of the Mouth. Erythroplakia is strongly associated with the use of tobacco and alcohol consumption, with some correlation associated with betel quid chewing. Contributed by H Olmo, DDS, MS</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="erythroplakia__2" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
        </fig>
      </floats-group>
      <floats-group id="article-136381.s19">
        <fig id="article-136381.image.f4" position="float" orientation="portrait">
          <caption>
            <p>Buccal Vestibule With Hyperkeratosis and Verrucous Carcinoma. Verrucous carcinoma is a low-grade variant of squamous cell carcinoma. While its etiology is not clearly defined, human papillomavirus, smoking, poor oral hygiene, lichenoid lesions, or chewing tobacco have been attributed to its causation. Contributed by H Olmo, DDS, MS</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="Verrucous__Carcinoma" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
        </fig>
      </floats-group>
      <floats-group id="article-136381.s20">
        <fig id="article-136381.image.f5" position="float" orientation="portrait">
          <caption>
            <p>Tongue, Lateral Border With Ulcerated Lesions. This image shows deep, red, ulcerated lesions on the lateral border of the tongue. Contributed by H Olmo, DDS, MS</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="SCC" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
        </fig>
      </floats-group>
